# TODO - Offline and multiplayer contracts

## Objective

Verify local and self-hosted play without commercial services.

## Acceptance

- Test host/join, local controllers, LAN clients and disconnect/rejoin.
- Bound and validate untrusted messages; default to local-only services.
- Require no central account for offline games.

## Evidence

Partial evidence, 2026-11-24: `cargo validate --no-cache` passes.
The shared `games::network::Session` policy supports local identities,
explicit opt-in LAN admission, bounded messages, reserved disconnect slots,
and same-origin reconnect. Title-specific codecs reject malformed remote
actions before simulation. Synthetic tests reject unknown identities,
excessive payloads, accidental LAN exposure and over-capacity joins.

The native `games-platform::lan` adapter now provides explicit private-address
TCP binding and bounded frames, with whole-transfer deadlines and connection
closure on invalid or incomplete wire data. Six loopback tests verify
bidirectional framing, opt-in, size and timeout handling, and composition
with session decoding and reconnect using test-controlled identities.
Fresh validation passed in run 1795573514614423045-2067685.

The native adapter now also supports mutually authenticated TLS 1.3 with
explicit local trust roots, server-name verification, leaf certificate
fingerprints and no session resumption. Raw TCP frames are test-only;
production code exposes only the secure adapter. Loopback tests verify
both certificate identities, secure frame boundaries, disconnect/rejoin,
rejection of a wrong host name and an untrusted client, and a bounded
handshake when an unauthenticated socket stops responding.

Fresh validation passed in run 1795576645026554056-2660129.
The tests provision temporary certificates; a real host must enrol trusted
fingerprints and bind them to player slots before admitting any messages.
No real multi-device LAN play or credential enrolment workflow is verified.

The host adapter now composes the shared roster and TLS stream ownership.
A locally configured, unique fingerprint-to-player mapping is bounded by
session capacity. A CA-trusted but unenrolled peer cannot join; neither a
duplicate connection nor a local controller can claim an enrolled identity.
Transport loss reserves the slot, and only the same approved certificate
can rejoin it. The host rejects mismatched frame limits and outbound
connections, applies the title-specific schema before returning a message,
and supports local controllers without any socket or account service.

Physical multi-device LAN play, real credential provisioning and integration
into a playable host remain open. The synchronous host adapter is intended
for an I/O worker; integration with the playable host is still needed.

Fresh validation passed in run 1795576800190768628-2685436 (78 tests).

The listener now limits outstanding unauthenticated sockets to the configured
player count. The permit is released on drop or handshake completion/failure.
A handshake uses the original accepted-socket deadline even after queueing.
Tests cover saturation, capacity recovery and rejection after queue expiry.
Fresh validation passed in run 1795576898196627474-2708567 (80 tests).

The client additionally requires a locally approved host leaf SHA-256
fingerprint during TLS authentication. Standard WebPKI certificate-chain,
name, validity and handshake-signature verification still apply. A different
leaf signed by the same trusted CA is rejected, as is a pinned leaf without
a trusted chain. Certificate rotation requires explicit local re-enrolment;
no production credential provisioning interface is claimed yet.
Fresh validation passed in run 1795577894972235875-2911264 (109 tests).

Host-side enrollment revocation drops active channels and releases both
connected and reserved player identities. Revoked certificates remain
ineligible for this host's application session even when a TLS handshake
can still authenticate their chain. Loopback tests cover active, disconnected,
never-connected and already-revoked identities. Fresh validation passed in
run 1795578187013800242-2949531 (127 workspace tests).

The shared input router now supports exclusive mappings for each attached
controller. Synthetic tests route four simultaneous controllers to distinct
player actions, reject fallback for unbound buttons on assigned devices,
and release old actions on reassignment or detach without cancelling other
held inputs. Window focus loss releases keyboard and touch holds while
preserving controller input. Native device integration remains pending.
